  "_sDescription": "Just like my mom's sweeper.",
  "_bGenerateTableOfContents": false,
  "_sText": "The Benelli M1014 JSCS or the\u00a0<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benelli_M4\" target=\"_blank\">Benelli M4</a> is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semi-automatic_shotgun\" target=\"_blank\">semi-automatic shotgun</a> produced by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy\" target=\"_blank\">Italian</a> firearm manufacturer <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benelli_Armi_SpA\" target=\"_blank\">Benelli Armi SpA</a>, and the last of the \"Benelli Super 90\" series of semi-automatic shotguns. The M4 uses a proprietary <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Action_(firearms)\" target=\"_blank\">action</a> design called the \"auto-regulating gas-operated\" (ARGO) system, which was created specifically for the weapon.\u00a0<br>The weapon was designed in 1998 and\u00a0is currently in service with the\u00a0<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army\" target=\"_blank\">United States Army</a>\u00a0and\u00a0<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Marine_Corps\" target=\"_blank\">Marine Corps</a>\u00a0(as the \"M1014\") as well as the United States Navy SEALs and the Los Angeles Police Department. The weapon has also been adopted by Australia, Georgia, Greece, Italy, Iraq, Ireland, Israel, Libya, Lithuania, Malaysia, Malta, Slovakia, Slovenia,\u00a0<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Kingdom\" target=\"_blank\">the United Kingdom</a>\u00a0(as the L128A1), and South Korea. Many of these groups stock the M4 for the ranks of their special forces.<br>The JSCS stands for \"Joint Services Combat Shotgun\", showing that this shotgun is widely employed by different armed force factions, and that's the reason sometimes the US Army may call the M1014 a \"JSCS\".<br>",
